# NCP IAM credentials for examples / smoke tests.
#
# This SDK targets NCP services across two auth tiers:
#   1. NCP HMAC v2 (67 services): use ncloudgo.NewHTTPClient(...)
#   2. AWS SigV4 (Object Storage): use ncloudgo.NewS3HTTPClient(...)
# Both tiers consume the same NCP IAM access-key/secret pair below —
# only the signing flow differs. So a single .env powers both.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill the two values. `.env` is in .gitignore;
# `.env.example` is committed.
NCLOUD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=ncp_iam_BPASKR...
NCLOUD_SECRET_KEY=ncp_iam_BPKSKR...

# Optional: region + environment. ncloudgo.LoadDefaultConfig consults
# these after programmatic options and before falling back to the
# shared config file (~/.config/ncloud-community/configure → DEFAULT
# profile) and finally to kr / public.
#
#   NCLOUD_REGION       — kr | sg | jp | de | usw   (default: kr)
#   NCLOUD_ENVIRONMENT  — public | financial | gov  (default: public)
#   NCLOUD_PROFILE      — section name in the shared config file
#                         (default: DEFAULT)
# NCLOUD_REGION=kr
# NCLOUD_ENVIRONMENT=public
# NCLOUD_PROFILE=DEFAULT

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Out of scope: other NCP service tiers
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The spec catalog (spec/services/) also contains:
#   - ncloud-app/   — Naver-branded apps with per-app/per-project secrets
#   - hmac-v1/      — legacy KMS v1 (HMAC v1 + APIGW key hybrid)
#   - swift-compat/ — Archive Storage (OpenStack Swift token auth)
#
# These are NOT generated into this SDK because each uses a credential
# model that cannot be unified with the IAM access-key/secret chain.
# If you want to call them, the auth/ package still ships building-block
# transports (auth.ClientKeyTransport, auth.BearerTransport,
# auth.HeadersTransport) that you can wire into a hand-rolled
# *http.Client. See auth/README.md for the full taxonomy and examples.
